---
title: About Bill Llia
order: 1
sectionType: bio
subtitle: A lifetime spent serving Nairobi's hardest-hit communities - from health clinics to the campaign for Governor. Bill Llia doesn't make promises he cannot keep.
icon: healthcare
---

Dr. Bill Llia has spent over a decade on the frontlines of Nairobi County — not in a government office, but in the communities where the need is greatest. He is a healthcare professional who has treated preventable diseases in homes without running water. A community organizer who has watched talented young people graduate into unemployment. A father who believes that no family in Nairobi should have to choose between buying medicine and buying food.

Bill began his career as a community health worker, walking door to door in the county's most underserved wards. He saw a mother lose her child to a disease that a simple vaccine would have prevented. He met a small business owner forced to close because a broken water pump made his products impossible to sell. He watched bright students drop out of school not because they lacked ability, but because their families lacked resources.

That is why he is running for Governor — not for the title, but for the chance to change those stories.

Under Bill's leadership, Nairobi County will be a place where a visit to the clinic does not mean a day lost to travel. Where a young person with a skill can find work. Where a farmer can get a fair price and a business owner can get a permit without paying a bribe. Where government works for the people who need it most.

When Bill Llia says "Service with integrity. Leadership with heart," he means every word — and his record proves it.
